{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And now you went, etc.</b> The explanation is that since beforehand he accepted the claim of why he hid in fleeing — holding him to be a fugitive — and afterward returned to say ״and now,״ meaning an expression of reply, as they of blessed memory said (Genesis Rabbah 21), and the intention is: and if you answer me that you did not flee, but rather ״went״ in the manner of walking you walked, <b>for you were sorely longing</b>, etc. — and not as I said to you in the manner of flight; if so, why did you steal my elohim? Rather, surely it must be that because he is an informant — lest he inform me and tell me that you went — you stole him, and this is your sign that you fled."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:17.572909833Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}